0.65]\n\u2022 Cost of equity = 4.70 + 0.60 \u00d7 4.50 = 7.40%\n\u2022 Pre-tax cost of debt = 5.0% [Assumption \u2014 A/A-rated pharma on 10Y+125-150bp] \u2192 after-tax 4.25% at 15% [Assumption]\n\u2022 Weights: E 88.3% / D 11.7% (EV $530.5B) [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 WACC = 7.0% [Arithmetic]\n\nPV of explicit FCFF (disc. at 7.0%): 21.0 + 21.9 + 22.0 + 22.0 + 21.3 + 20.0 + 18.8 + 15.5 + 12.1 + 9.6 = 184.2\nTerminal: FCFF 2036E = 18.8 \u00d7 1.01 = 19.0, g=1.0% [Assumption]; TV = 19.0 / (0.070\u22120.010) = 316.7; PV = 161.0\nEV = 345.2 | +cash 5.2 \u2212 debt 67.5 = $283.0 equity | /1.767B sh = $160/share (BASE CASE)\n\nCross-checks:\n\u2022 Forward adjusted P/E: $264.96 / $13.97 mid-FY26E = 19.0x \u2014 vs big pharma peers 11-15x; premium is 30-70%; PEG = 19.0/16.2 = 1.17 (fair, not cheap) [Arithmetic + consensus]\n\u2022 EV/sales: $530.5B / $64.4B TTM = 8.2x vs peer ~4-5x \u2014 rich [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Reverse-DCF at $265: implied perpetuity FCFF at 7% = $530.5B \u00d7 7% = $37.1B \u2014 requires FCFF to compound to $37B by 2035, implying revenue/margin beyond my base case and no real cliff [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Buffer: If WACC is 6.0% (beta 0.45), base IV rises to \u2248 $204 [Sensitivity]. The market is effectively pricing a 6% WACC + bull pipeline \u2014 a combination that lacks margin of safety.\n\nTornado Top-3 (from \u00b11\u03c3 sensitivity):\n1. Loss-of-exclusivity date (2033 tested vs 2037): swings IV by \u00b145%\n2. WACC (6.0% vs 7.0%): swings IV by \u00b125%\n3. Peak adjusted EBIT margin (\u00b12pp): swings IV by \u00b112%\n\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Competitive response: Lilly's oral IL-23 and JAK competitors, biosimilar developers entering at 2033 \u2014 expected price competition (-2).\n\u2022 Reflexivity: strong FCF funds dividend and pipeline; no reflexive reliance on stock price \u2014 positive for stability.\n\u2022 Customer behavior: chronic immunology patients sticky through mid-exclusivity; late-adopter penetration in IBD unlocks Skyrizi's $20B+ peak [Estimate].\n\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior base rate anchors: LOE handoff success ~40%; large-M&A ROIC>WACC ~30%; quality compounder survival >90%. Local company-specific evidence (Humira execution, settlement wins) updates the prior moderately upward.\n\nScenario A \u2014 BEAR (25%): Early biosimilar pressure 2029-2030; Apogee/Cerevel write-off; no pipeline offset; WACC 7.5%.\nPrice: $103 [IV]\nScenario B \u2014 BASE (50%): 2033 cliff as modeled; moderate pipeline offset; WACC 7.0%.\nPrice: $170 [IV]\nScenario C \u2014 BULL (25%): Rinvoq settlements hold; US erosion starts 2034; pipeline covers 50% of lost revenues; WACC 6.5%.\nPrice: $293 [IV]\n\nWeighted intrinsic value = 0.25\u00d7103 + 0.50\u00d7170 + 0.25\u00d7293 = $184/share [Arithmetic]\n50% CI: $138-$232 [Estimate] | 80% CI: $103-$293 [Scenario bounds]\nMargin of safety vs T0: (184 \u2212 264.96) / 184 = -44% \u2192 NONE.\nIf I bias the bull case up (40% bull/15% bear): EV = $209 \u2014 still -21% below price. Conclusion is robust to that re-weighting.\n\n\nSECTION 4.5. HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMarket-implied horizon: ~8-10 years of growth (based on 19x forward EPS and reverse-DCF requirements). My horizon: 3-5 years. Spread at current pricing: the market price reaches far beyond my high-confidence visibility (2026 guidance only); the market is paying multiple years ahead of the evidence on Apogee and post-2033 replacement. Time-horizon arbitrage: NEGATIVE \u2014 the \"arbitrage\" favors the patient seller, not the buyer.\n\n\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nConviction score (0-3 per category):\nBusiness quality: 3 | Valuation attractiveness: 1 | Macro alignment: 1 | Thesis clarity: 3 | Execution traceability: 2 \u2192 10/15.\nMacro headwind: -0.5 \u2192 9.5/15 \u2192 MEDIUM conviction.\nConviction decay: -1 per 6 months absent confirming news on Apogee/pipeline.\nPosition sizing: no new purchase warranted; MAX weight 0-2% for existing holders at a \"core hold\" level. No new-money sizing at T0.\nLayer 5 vs 6.5 gap check: Kelly says 0%; Conviction-sizing maximum 2%. Gap < 20pp [within discipline]. No re-analysis needed.\n\n\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Short interest: 1.42% of float, 22.5M shares, DTC 3.69 \u2014 benign; no squeeze dynamic [Actual]\n\u2022 Institutional ownership: 78.45% \u2014 heavily held; ETF-flow vulnerability moderate [Actual]\n\u2022 Insider: 0.11% \u2014 negligible signal [Actual]\n\u2022 Options/sentiment: not available individually [Unconfirmed]; aggregate analyst mean $276.41, median $280, high $328, low $200 \u2014 Wall Street optimistic (mean +4.3% upside) [Actual, vendor]\n\u2022 Crowding score: 6/15 (moderate \u2014 consensus bullish, near 52-wk high $267.47, low short interest) \u2192 no size reduction penalty to existing holders; a caution flag against new entry.\n\n\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u