FY26 EPS ($13.87-14.07 guide already cut $0.04).\n\n\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Common portfolio bear trigger: rising 10Y (the current macro regime) is a shared risk with any other long-duration/high-multiple name; ABBV is 2-3x more sensitive than the market average on rate beta. If portfolio holds MSFT/COST/PLTR alongside ABBV, the regime is the single point of failure.\n\u2022 Tail correlation: 2008/2020/2022 style stress sees ABBV fall with equities (defensive only in 2020; fell with rates in 2022).\n\u2022 CVaR estimate (5% tail): ~-35% in a 2022-like repricing (from $265 \u2192 ~$172) [Estimate].\n\n\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nThesis integrity thresholds (KPI = Skyrizi+Rinvoq combined, Apogee milestones, FY27 guide):\n1. If combined Skyrizi+Rinvoq 12-mo revenue growth drops below +8%, downgrade thesis to base-case fade.\n2. If Skyrizi/Rinvoq selected for IRA 2028+ round [Unconfirmed \u2192 monitor], re-run valuation with -12% Medicare explicit haircut.\n3. If Apogee Phase 2 OX40L misses, write off $10.9B deal in DCF (reduce terminal value ~8%).\n4. If 10Y > 5.25%, re-run WACC at +50bp and re-evaluate full position.\n5. Pre-mortem: \"If ABBV fails in 5 years, likely cause = early biosimilar entry 2029 + pipeline gap + debt-funded M&A failure.\" Early indicators: biosimilar settlement news, clinical holds, Moody's/S&P downgrade to BBB, Skyrizi script deceleration 3 consecutive quarters.\n\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM \u2014 SHORT THESIS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n1. Historical precedent: Humira fell from $21.6B peak to ~$8B; Skyrizi/Rinvoq face the same mechanism in 2033 (or sooner) \u2014 50-70% peak drop is the drug-class rule.\n2. Market is paying 19x forward adjusted EPS and ~26x FCF for a company whose two growth products supply >50% of revenue \u2014 peak multiples on cliff-bound assets are the classic value trap.\n3. IRA selection is expanding; Skyrizi/Rinvoq have high Medicare exposure and are obvious future targets.\n4. M&A record is mixed: Cerevel's lead asset failed; Apogee adds $10.9B cost with no revenue for 3+ years.\n5. Consensus $276 mean target = the market already believes the bull case; no upside surprise left unless pipeline over-delivers.\n6. Dividend is $12.2B/yr requiring 100%+ of adjusted FCF at some points post-Apogee close, constraining balance sheet optionality.\n7. Macro: 4.7% 10Y + possibly hawkish Fed = re-rating risk for a long-duration compounder.\n\nLogic combat (Long vs Short): Long: +10% near-term growth, Humira-proof execution, wide moat, 2.1x net debt/EBITDA, $18B+ FCF. Short: premium multiple, cliff at 2033, IRA tail, M&A failure risk. Gap < 2 points \u2014 the short logic is strong and based on the SAME data. Conviction downgraded accordingly (already reflected).\n\nAdversarial data check: no Hindenburg/recent activist report found in limited search [Unconfirmed]; largest counter-risk is data I could not access (full Q&A transcript, 2028 IRA list contents).\n\nKilled arguments (and revival conditions):\n\u2022 \"Settlements hold Rinvoq to 2037\" \u2014 dismissed as no-entry edge (already priced by market); revives if the settlement collapses in court (litigation risk).\n\u2022 \"2027 revenue $31B for Skyrizi+Rinvoq\" is strong \u2014 but does not establish 2030+ sustainability.\n\u2022 \"Management raised FY26 guidance twice\" \u2014 priced in; does not address FY27+.\n\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nA. Methodology: Engine 1, 10-yr explicit + terminal; peer cross-check included; DCF not stand-alone. PASS.\nB. Valuation: reverse-DCF and multiples reconcile; biggest uncertainty flagged as LOE timing instead of being silently assumed. PASS.\nC. Bias: bear/bull symmetric and explicitly sourced; base case is NOT the highest-return scenario; audit sought negative evidence. PASS.\nD. Consistency: FCFF definition consistent with capex\u2248depreciation logic; no mixing of GAAP/adjusted earnings. PASS.\nE. Narrative: no TAM narrative, no \"platform premium\", no vague optionality; pipeline claims limited to me-too phase, data-tagged. PASS.\nF. Red team: executed; short logic within 2 pts of long logic \u2192 conviction downgraded. PASS.\nG. Data integrity: pack series continuity warning addressed (2020 Allergan step-up, no 2015 revenue-style defect identified); adjusted-vs-GAAP margins tied to vendor and clearly [Estimate]; unable to independently verify 2028 IRA list contents [Unconfirmed]. PASS WITH DISCLOSURES.\n\nSECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDate/T0: 2026-08-24 | Price: $264.96 | Mkt cap: $468.2B\nKey inputs: FY26 rev guide $67.6B; FY26 adj EPS guide $13.87-14.07; WACC 7.0%; LOE start 2033; terminal g 1%.\nBase IV: $170 | Probability-weighted IV: $184 | 80% CI: $103-$293.\nMargin of safety: none (expected -31% vs market).\nRed team concern: market is paying bull-case without bull-case evidence; the 19x forward P/E discounts the 2033 cliff as if it won't happen.\nAssumption ledger: LOE timing (2033 not 2028/2037); WACC 7.0% vs market implied ~6%; adjusted margins; pipeline offset; taxes.\n\nSECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nACTION: HOLD (if owned) / DO NOT INITIATE (no new exposure). \nCONVICTION: Medium (9.5/15).\nWEIGHT: 0% for new money; trim existing positions sized above 2% of portfolio; core holders cap at 1-2% and let the dividend carry the carry.\nSTRATEGY:\n\u2022 Limit orders stand at $150-185 (30-45% MoS from probability-weighted IV); scale entries 3 tranches.\n\u2022 Buy zone rationale: at \u2264$185, expected value becomes positive with +10% upside to weighted IV and the dividend yield rises toward 3.7-4.6%, restoring the defensive-contractor role.\n\u2022 Existing holders: consider trimming above $265 only if thesis KPI (Skyrizi+Rinvoq growth) decelerates or 10Y rises >5.25%; otherwise hold and collect $6.92 dividend.\n\u2022 Critical re-evaluation triggers: 2028 IRA list (is Skyrizi/Rinvoq selected?), Q4 2026 FY27 guide, Apogee Phase 2 data, Rinvoq settlement legal outcome.\n\nSUMMARY: Wonderful business, wrong price. At $264.96 the market is allocating capital as if the 2033 exclusivity cliff is a low-probability tail event; the base rate of drug-class cliffs suggests the opposite. ABBV deserves a place in a diversified portfolio \u2014 but only after the price grants a margin of safety, or after the company demonstrates a credible post-2033 growth engine that exceeds the current line-of-sight.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u