e raised; Apogee announced |\n| Base IV | $206 (DCF) / $215\u2013225 (blended) |\n| Scenario E[P] | $226 |\n| Key assumptions | WACC 7.2%; terminal g 1.5%; 2026\u201330 EPS path $14.18\u2192$16.41; FCF conversion 95%\u219291%; total debt $67.9B; Medicare selection NOT in base |\n| Red-team concern | 2033 LOE is the structural cliff; Apogee M&A; Medicare 2028 list |\n| Discipline rule | Do not initiate above $240; trim to \u22642% if held; buy zone $220\u2013235; re-evaluate at CMS list release, Apogee data, or any Skyrizi settlement news |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 12 \u2014 FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\n- **Action: HOLD (if owned) / DO NOT INITIATE at $264.96.**\n- **Conviction: Medium (8\u20139/15).**\n- **Weight: 0\u20132% for existing holders; 0% for new money.**\n- **Strategy:**\n  1. Staircase accumulation only in the **$228\u2013238** zone (first tranche at \u2264$238), with maximum position 2%.\n  2. If held, consider a **covered-call overlay** at the $280 strike (2027 expiry) to augment the 2.67% dividend yield and reduce effective entry cost.\n  3. **Hard sell triggers:** adjusted EPS guide cut \u22653% below $14.08; Skyrizi+Rinvoq growth <10% for two quarters; net debt/EBITDA >3.5x; CMS 2028 list includes Rinvoq \u2014 re-evaluate immediately, likely sharp thesis downgrade.\n  4. **Re-rating upside is real but not free:** buying at $265 requires 2030 EPS \u2265$19\u201320 and no margin compression \u2014 that is the bull case (25% probability), not the base case. The market is paying for success; wait for a better price.\n- **Sponsor-grade bottom line:** An excellent business, a good balance sheet-by-pharma-standards, and an attractive dividend \u2014 but **zero margin of safety today**. The asymmetry is negative. Patient investors should build the position only on a pullback toward $220\u2013235 (which would restore a meaningful 5\u201310% MoS vs base case).\n\n```"}, {"sample": 2, "iv": 210.0, "plausible": true, "reasons": [], "flags": [], "truncated": false, "