ance only); the market is paying multiple years ahead of the evidence on Apogee and post-2033 replacement. Time-horizon arbitrage: NEGATIVE \u2014 the \"arbitrage\" favors the patient seller, not the buyer.\n\n\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nConviction score (0-3 per category):\nBusiness quality: 3 | Valuation attractiveness: 1 | Macro alignment: 1 | Thesis clarity: 3 | Execution traceability: 2 \u2192 10/15.\nMacro headwind: -0.5 \u2192 9.5/15 \u2192 MEDIUM conviction.\nConviction decay: -1 per 6 months absent confirming news on Apogee/pipeline.\nPosition sizing: no new purchase warranted; MAX weight 0-2% for existing holders at a \"core hold\" level. No new-money sizing at T0.\nLayer 5 vs 6.5 gap check: Kelly says 0%; Conviction-sizing maximum 2%. Gap < 20pp [within discipline]. No re-analysis needed.\n\n\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Short interest: 1.42% of float, 22.5M shares, DTC 3.69 \u2014 benign; no squeeze dynamic [Actual]\n\u2022 Institutional ownership: 78.45% \u2014 heavily held; ETF-flow vulnerability moderate [Actual]\n\u2022 Insider: 0.11% \u2014 negligible signal [Actual]\n\u2022 Options/sentiment: not available individually [Unconfirmed]; aggregate analyst mean $276.41, median $280, high $328, low $200 \u2014 Wall Street optimistic (mean +4.3% upside) [Actual, vendor]\n\u2022 Crowding score: 6/15 (moderate \u2014 consensus bullish, near 52-wk high $267.47, low short interest) \u2192 no size reduction penalty to existing holders; a caution flag against new entry.\n\n\nSE